ate winter and early spring. Maple trees are tapped by drilling holes into their trunks and collecting the sap, which is heated to evaporate much of the water, leaving the concentrated syrup."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-maple-syrup"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maple_syrup"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Pumpkin pie","dish/pumpkin-pie"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Allspice","ingredient/allspice"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Cinnamon","ingredient/cinnamon"],["Clove","ingredient/clove"],["Condensed milk","ingredient/condensed-milk"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Nutmeg","ingredient/nutmeg"],["Pumpkin","ingredient/pumpkin"],["Shortcrust pastry","ingredient/shortcrust-pastry"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Mentioned in","links":[["Anishinaabe foodways","cuisine/anishinaabe-foodways"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/1/18/Maple_syrup.jpg/500px-Maple_syrup.jpg","w":500,"h":994,"by":"User:Miguel Andrade","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maple_syrup.jpg"}},"dish/rubaboo":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/rubaboo","n":"Rubaboo","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Métis foodways","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["A ",["Métis","cuisine/metis-foodways"]," stew, traditionally of peas or corn with grease, a thickener and ",["Pemmican","dish/pemmican"],". Later versions use rabbit, chicken or sage hen with wild vegetables."]],"src":"note","sources":[{"name":"Gabriel Dumont Institute, Traditional Métis foods","url":"https://www.metismuseum.ca/media/document.php/14522.Traditional Metis Foods revised May 2018.pdf"}],"actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-rubaboo"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rubaboo"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Métis foodways","cuisine/metis-foodways"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Maize","ingredient/maize"],["Pea","ingredient/pea"]]},{"h":"More from Métis foodways","links":[["Bannock (Indigenous American food)","dish/bannock-indigenous-american-food"],["Pemmican","dish/pemmican"]]}]}}